on her visit to china angela merkel is  trying to strike a balance between  business deals and human rights  at a meeting with president xi jinping  the chancellor promoted an innovative  bilateral partnership that would connect  german sino trade deals with chinese  political reform such as greater civil  liberty  it also includes other areas of  cooperation such as societal development  the development of the legal social and  educational systems  although that has not been agreed  several deals have been closed during  merkel's visit  volkswagen was one of the companies to  sign a contract to build two new plants  in china with a local partner  chinese economic growth may be slowing  but premier lee kichang said what is  most needed is reform not stimulus  china is still on the path to  modernization first and foremost that  means fundamental economic restructuring  he said beijing wants to see a broader  distribution of wealth and do more to  support smaller businesses  that approach will open new avenues for  german business  talks between beijing and berlin are  ongoing with the next government level  meetings planned for october  you
 

